# WorldScope — Cursor Agent Rules & Build Plan
> Flutter Technical Assessment | 3 Levels | Target: ~3 hours
> Read this file fully before writing any code. Follow phases in order.

---

## Project Overview

Build **WorldScope**, a multi-feature Flutter mobile app (Android) consuming 4 public REST APIs across 3 levels. Code must be clean, explainable, and working. Commit after every phase.

**APIs summary:**
| API | Key? | Used in |
|---|---|---|
| restcountries.com/v3.1 | No | L1 + L3 |
| open-meteo.com | No | L2 + L3 |
| api.opencagedata.com | Yes — inject from env | L2 |
| newsapi.org | Yes — inject from env | L3 |

---

## Ground Rules (Never Break These)

- Flutter + Dart only. No low-code tools.
- Must run on Android. Test on emulator frequently.
- No business logic inside `build()` methods — ever.
- All API calls use `async/await` with proper error handling.
- Every field from the API must be null-safe with a readable fallback string.
- Commit message format: `level1-phase2: data layer` etc.
- At least 3 service classes by Level 3: `CountryService`, `WeatherService`, `NewsService`.

