# LEVEL 3 — News + Country Deep-Dive

**Target time: 60 minutes**
**APIs:** All 4 (REST Countries + OpenCage + Open-Meteo + NewsAPI)

---

## L3 Phase 1 — News Model + Service (10 min)

### `lib/models/news_article.dart`
Fields: `String title`, `String? description`, `String url`, `String? urlToImage`, `String source`

Parse from `articles[]` array in NewsAPI response.

### `lib/services/news_service.dart`

```dart
class NewsService {
  static const _base = 'https://newsapi.org/v2/top-headlines';
  static const _key = 'YOUR_KEY_HERE';

  Future<List<NewsArticle>> fetchHeadlines(String countryCode2) async {
    // NewsAPI uses 2-letter codes (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2)
    final uri = Uri.parse('$_base?country=${countryCode2.toLowerCase()}&pageSize=5&apiKey=$_key');
    final res = await http.get(uri);
    if (res.statusCode != 200) throw Exception('News fetch failed');
    final data = jsonDecode(res.body);
    final articles = data['articles'] as List? ?? [];
    return articles.map((a) => NewsArticle.fromJson(a)).toList();
  }
}
```

Note: REST Countries gives `cca2` (2-letter) and `cca3` (3-letter). Use `cca2` for NewsAPI.

Update `CountrySummary` model to also include `cca2` field.

---

## L3 Phase 2 — Deep Dive Screen Shell (10 min)

### `lib/screens/deep_dive_screen.dart` — StatefulWidget

Constructor: `final CountrySummary country`

State:
```dart
CountryDetail? _detail;
WeatherModel? _weather;
List<NewsArticle> _news = [];
bool _loading = true;
Map<String, String?> _errors = {'country': null, 'weather': null, 'news': null};
```

`initState()` → call `_loadAll()`

**Critical — use `Future.wait` for parallel calls:**
```dart
Future<void> _loadAll() async {
  setState(() => _loading = true);
  final results = await Future.wait([
    CountryService().fetchByCode(country.cca3).then((d) => _detail = d).catchError((e) {
      _errors['country'] = e.toString(); return null;
    }),
    _loadWeather(country).catchError((e) {
      _errors['weather'] = e.toString(); return null;
    }),
    NewsService().fetchHeadlines(country.cca2).then((n) => _news = n).catchError((e) {
      _errors['news'] = e.toString(); return null;
    }),
  ], eagerError: false); // eagerError: false → don't stop on first failure
  setState(() => _loading = false);
}

Future<void> _loadWeather(CountrySummary c) async {
  final capital = // get from detail or use country name as fallback
  final w = await WeatherService().getWeatherForCity(capital);
  _weather = w;
}
```

`build()`: if `_loading` → spinner. Else → `DefaultTabController(length: 3)` with:
- `TabBar`: Country Info | Weather | News
- `TabBarView`: 3 tabs

---

## L3 Phase 3 — Three Tabs (15 min)

### Tab 1 — Country Info
Reuse `CountryDetailScreen` layout content. If `_errors['country'] != null` → show error text. Else show all 5 fields.

### Tab 2 — Weather
If `_errors['weather'] != null` → show error. Else show current weather + 7-day scroll (reuse `WeatherCard` widget).

### Tab 3 — News
If `_errors['news'] != null` → show "No news available".
If `_news.isEmpty` → show "No news available for this country".
Else: `ListView` of `NewsTile` widgets.

### `lib/widgets/news_tile.dart`
`ListTile`:
- `title`: headline text
- `subtitle`: source name
- `onTap`: `launchUrl(Uri.parse(article.url))` using `url_launcher`

---

