## Critical Implementation Notes

### Null safety patterns
```dart
// currencies map: {"USD": {"name": "Dollar", "symbol": "$"}}
final currencies = json['currencies'] as Map<String, dynamic>?;
final firstCurrency = currencies?.values.first;
final currencyName = firstCurrency?['name'] ?? 'N/A';
final currencySymbol = firstCurrency?['symbol'] ?? '';

// languages map: {"eng": "English", "fra": "French"}
final languages = (json['languages'] as Map?)?.values.join(', ') ?? 'N/A';

// capital is an array
final capital = (json['capital'] as List?)?.first ?? 'N/A';
```

### Error widget pattern (reuse everywhere)
```dart
// lib/widgets/error_widget.dart
class AppErrorWidget extends StatelessWidget {
  final String message;
  final VoidCallback? onRetry;
  // ...
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Center(
    child: Column(mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min, children: [
      Icon(Icons.error_outline, size: 48, color: Colors.red),
      SizedBox(height: 8),
      Text(message, textAlign: TextAlign.center),
      if (onRetry != null) TextButton(onPressed: onRetry, child: Text('Retry')),
    ]),
  );
}
```

### SharedPreferences pattern
```dart
// Save
final prefs = await SharedPreferences.getInstance();
await prefs.setString('last_city', city);

// Load
final prefs = await SharedPreferences.getInstance();
final lastCity = prefs.getString('last_city');
if (lastCity != null) _search(lastCity);
```

### Future.wait error isolation (Level 3)
```dart
// Use catchError on each future so one failure doesn't cancel others
await Future.wait([
  apiCall1().catchError((e) { _errors['key1'] = e.toString(); }),
  apiCall2().catchError((e) { _errors['key2'] = e.toString(); }),
  apiCall3().catchError((e) { _errors['key3'] = e.toString(); }),
], eagerError: false);
```

### url_launcher setup
Add to `android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml` inside `<manifest>`:
```xml
<queries>
  <intent>
    <action android:name="android.intent.action.VIEW" />
    <data android:scheme="https" />
  </intent>
</queries>
```

